<section class="section science" id="science" aria-labelledby="science-title">
  <h2 id="science-title">The science behind the technique</h2>
  <p class="science__lede">
    Shadowing has decades of research behind it. It's one of the most studied
    pronunciation training methods in second language acquisition.
  </p>
  <div class="stats">
    <div class="stat">
      <b>30-40%</b>
      <span class="src">Hamada, 2016 · Language Teaching Research</span>
      <p>Better listening comprehension. Lower-proficiency learners showed the largest gains in phoneme perception and word recognition.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="stat">
      <b>25%</b>
      <span class="src">Foote &amp; McDonough, 2017 · J. of Second Language Pronunciation</span>
      <p>More accurate pronunciation. Mobile-based shadowing produced significant gains in prosodic fluency, intonation and rhythm.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="stat">
      <b>82%</b>
      <span class="src">Trần Văn Hòa, 2020</span>
      <p>Reported less speaking anxiety. Consistent practice built confidence in students who previously avoided speaking.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
